{#
  The furniture every notebook post carries, defined ONCE.

    postHeader       the date, the <h1>, then the back link, in one bordered
                     block. The link sits UNDER the title so the first thing on
                     the page is the page's own name.
    postHeaderBlock  postHeader in its own text column, for a layout whose body
                     is full width.
    postEnding       the closing date rule and the "← NOTEBOOK FRONT PAGE" link.

  Used by:
    post.njk                        markdown posts (input_markdown/)
    post_body.njk                   block posts (input_custom_post/), which
                                    includes every page-builder export
    eleventy_njk/_builder_shell.njk the page builder's preview shell, called
                                    with {{TOKEN}} strings the app fills in

  The page builder emits NONE of this markup itself; its exports are hero +
  content only. So a change here reaches every post, the builder's preview and
  its editor on the next build, and there is no second copy to keep in step.

  Every value is an argument, never read from the page context, so the shell
  can pass placeholder tokens where a post passes real values. That is also why
  the dates arrive already formatted: the shell has no date to format.

  post_body.njk rejects (at build time, in eleventy.config.js) a body that
  carries its own "← NOTEBOOK FRONT PAGE" link. If that text changes here,
  change it there too.
#}

{% macro postHeader(title, dateIso, dateHuman) %}
<div class="mb-8 pb-8 border-b border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800">
    <time class="text-sm font-mono text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 uppercase tracking-wider" datetime="{{ dateIso }}">
        {{ dateHuman }}
    </time>
    {#- No title, no heading: an empty <h1> is still an <h1> to a screen reader. #}
    {%- if title %}
    <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-6xl text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-4 uppercase tracking-wider">
        {{ title }}
    </h1>
    {%- endif %}
    <a href="/notebook" class="inline-flex items-center text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 hover:text-neutral-900 dark:hover:text-white transition-colors font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-wider">
       ← Back to Notebook
    </a>
</div>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro postHeaderBlock(title, dateIso, dateHuman) %}
<div class="post-container pt-24 fade_effect">
    {{ postHeader(title, dateIso, dateHuman) }}
</div>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro postEnding(dateIso, dateHuman) %}
<div class="post-container pt-24">
  <hr>
  <div class="py-2">
    <time class="text-sm font-mono text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 uppercase tracking-wider" datetime="{{ dateIso }}">
        {{ dateHuman }}
    </time>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="post-container pt-6">
    <a href="/notebook" class="inline-block border-b-2 border-black dark:border-white pb-1 hover:opacity-50 transition text-lg tracking-widest">
      ← NOTEBOOK FRONT PAGE
    </a>
</div>
{% endmacro %}
